In Python, with libraries such as NumPy and PyTorch, floating-point tensors are represented as arrays in memory. Each element of the array corresponds to a single value in the tensor. The dimensions of the tensor are defined by the shape of the array. For example, a 2D tensor with shape (3, 4) would be represented as a 3x4 array.

