4. Cross-lingual transfer learning: To evaluate the ability of an LLM to transfer knowledge between languages, it can be trained on data from one language and then evaluated on a different language. This can help to assess the model's generalization abilities across languages.

5. Probing tasks: Probing tasks are used to investigate the internal representations learned by LLMs and to evaluate their ability to capture language-specific features. For example, a probing task might involve asking the LLM to identify the tense or part of speech of a word in a sentence. These tasks can provide insights into the models' language-learning abilities and help to identify areas for improvement.
