Optimizing inference on edge devices involves tailoring algorithms and models to the specific hardware and resource constraints of the device. One approach is to use specialized hardware such as neural processors or tensor processing units (TPUs) that are optimized for machine learning tasks. Another approach is to use smaller, more efficient models such as MobileNet or SqueezeNet for image recognition, or smaller versions of Transformers for natural language processing tasks.

